{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "d7d794f7-c2a7-8e80-ba72-aa939307e212",
  "created_at": "2026-01-13T12:32:58-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Daniel Nguyen",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Luis Barros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:30:47-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Finance department, this is Luis. Happy Tuesday, such as it is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:30:51-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello. Yes, good afternoon. My name is Daniel Nguyen. I am calling about my property tax. I have a few questions, I wrote them down."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:00-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good, written down is the best way. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:04-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "First question. When is my next installment due? And does the city mail a reminder, or do I need to remember the date myself?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:12-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tax bills are quarterly, so there's a next installment coming up. Without your account in front of me I can't give you the exact day. The date is printed on your bill. As for reminders, the bill itself is the notice. I wouldn't count on a separate reminder showing up. I'd put the date on your calendar."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:31-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So the bill is the notice. I understand. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:35-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep. Next one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:37-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Second question. What are the office hours for the assessor's office?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:41-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They keep regular City Hall weekday hours, so Monday through Friday, daytime. Closed weekends and holidays. If you want to go in person, call ahead that morning just to be safe."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:31:52-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, weekdays, daytime. Good. Third, I want to set up an electronic check from my bank. I have the routing number here. Can I read it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:01-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, go ahead, nice and slow."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:04-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The routing number is three, zero, seven, two, one, seven, six, two, six."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:09-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three-zero-seven-two-one-seven-six-two-six. I have that. I'll need your account number for the tax bill too, and the bank account number, but we can do that part in a second."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I have the tax account number also. [pause] One moment. I am finding the page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:25-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Take your time. I'm not going anywhere. It's lunch hour and the phone's been quiet."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:31-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Also I should say, my mother-in-law is visiting from out of state this week, so I may be a little busy. If the call is cut, I will call again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:42-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. If we get cut off, call back and ask for me. Okay, read me the tax account number when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:50-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. The account number is four, four, one, eight, zero, two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:32:54-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-four-one-eight-zero-two. Got it. Now the bank account number."
    }
  ],
